/-!
# Distinct conjugates in the inner M₁₂ involution row

The displayed words give 320 conjugates of the original marked involution.
Five permutation values encode each conjugate. Kernel checks compare those
values with a strictly increasing integer table, proving distinctness.
Only a lower bound on the conjugacy class is needed for E.6.23; no
exhaustion or centralizer isomorphism is assumed. The generator tables are
checked against the original Witt-design/ATLAS permutations.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith 16.1.5(4), used in E.6.23.
-/

